### Case: okta-token-issue — obtain an access token FROM OKTA, not from the gateway.
### The gateway is not involved in this request at all. That is the whole point of
### this solution: Okta is the issuer, the gateway is only a verifier.
### Expect 200 with an RS256-signed JWT access_token.
POST {{OKTA_TOKEN_URL}}
authorization: Basic {{BASE64(OKTA_CLIENT_ID:OKTA_CLIENT_SECRET)}}
content-type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&scope={{OKTA_SCOPE}}

### curl equivalent:
###   curl -i -X POST {{OKTA_TOKEN_URL}} \
###     -u '{{OKTA_CLIENT_ID}}:{{OKTA_CLIENT_SECRET}}' \
###     -d 'grant_type=client_credentials' -d 'scope={{OKTA_SCOPE}}'
